# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE suppression list
# Add one CVE-ID per line to suppress accepted-risk findings.
# Each entry MUST include a justification comment and review date.

# CVE-2026-34483 — Tomcat information disclosure via JsonAccessLogValve encoding
# CVE-2026-34487 — Tomcat information disclosure via sensitive data in log files
# Both fixed in Tomcat 11.0.21. Spring Boot 4.0.5 ships Tomcat 11.0.20.
# Remove when Boot 4.0.6+ (Tomcat 11.0.21+) is released.
# Review: 2026-06-01
CVE-2026-34483
CVE-2026-34487

# CVE-2026-41284 — Tomcat HIGH: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling
# CVE-2026-41293 — Tomcat CRITICAL: Improper Input Validation
# CVE-2026-42498 — Tomcat: HTTP Authentication Header exposure during WebSocket upgrade
# CVE-2026-43512 — Tomcat: Authentication Bypass in digest auth (DEPRECATED upstream)
# CVE-2026-43513 — Tomcat: Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity in LockOutRealm
# All in org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core shipped by Spring Boot 4.1.0-RC1.
# Boot 4.1 will pull a patched Tomcat once 11.0.21+ propagates through the BOM.
# Accepted as residual risk for the demo cluster:
#   - All endpoints require Bearer API key or OAuth (ApiKeyFilter at chain top, no
#     anonymous auth surface for 43512 digest-auth bypass)
#   - RateLimiterFilter caps the resource-exhaustion vector for 41284
#   - WebSocket upgrade not exposed by any MCP tool (42498 inert in current config)
#   - Cluster behind OVH LoadBalancer, no public ingress for unauthenticated paths
# Remove when Spring Boot 4.1 GA ships with Tomcat 11.0.21+.
# Review: 2026-07-01
CVE-2026-41284
CVE-2026-41293
CVE-2026-42498
CVE-2026-43512
CVE-2026-43513
